.SH "NAME"
nvme-keys-check-kxchap-secret \- Check a host KX\-HMAC\-CHAP secret
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
\fInvme\fR [<global\-options>] \fIkeys check\-kxchap\-secret\fR [\-\-keydata=<secret> | \-d <secret>]
                        [\-\-keyring=<name> | \-k <name>]
                        [\-\-keytype=<type> | \-t <type>]
                        [\-\-identity=<identity> | \-i <identity>]
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Checks if the given string is a valid KX\-HMAC\-CHAP host secret of the form: DHHC\-1:00:ia6zGodOr4SEG0Zzaw398rpY0wqipUWj4jWjUh4HWUz6aQ2n: and prints the hash algorithm it records, the secret length, and the CRC\&.
.sp
If \fI\-\-keydata\fR is not given the secret is read from stdin, which also allows checking a secret stored in a file, e\&.g\&. \fInvme keys check\-kxchap\-secret < keyfile\fR\&.
.sp
If \fI\-\-identity\fR is given the specified keyring is also checked for a secret already stored under that identity (as inserted by \fBnvme-keys-import\fR(1)); the result (not loaded, loaded and matching, or loaded but different) is reported\&. This command never modifies the keyring\&.
.sp
Looking up a secret requires the \fIkxchap\fR keyring key type, which is not yet provided by any released Linux kernel; see \fBnvme-keys-import\fR(1) for details\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\-d <secret>, \-\-keydata=<secret>
.RS 4
Secret to be checked\&. If not given, the secret is read from stdin\&.
.RE
.PP
\-k <name>, \-\-keyring=<name>
.RS 4
Name of the keyring to check for an already loaded secret\&. Default is
\fI\&.nvme\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\-t <type>, \-\-keytype=<type>
.RS 4
Key type of the secret to look up\&. Default is
\fIkxchap\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\-i <identity>, \-\-identity=<identity>
.RS 4
Identity to look up in the keyring to check if the secret is already loaded\&. If not given, only the secret format is validated\&.
.RE
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.sp
The following options are defined at the top\-level nvme command and are available to this subcommand:
.PP
